WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.377
Operational security begins with protecting the workstation itself.

00:00:03.377 --> 00:00:06.244
Apply operating-system, browser, application, and extension updates.

00:00:06.244 --> 00:00:09.930
Use supported endpoint protection, a host firewall, screen locking,

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.026
and physical safeguards appropriate to the sensitivity of the work.

00:00:14.026 --> 00:00:20.170
Use unique passwords stored in an approved password manager and enable multi-factor authentication where available.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:23.037
Recovery methods should be controlled and documented.

00:00:23.037 --> 00:00:25.904
Do not place case credentials, API keys,

00:00:25.904 --> 00:00:29.590
or sensitive notes in browser scripts or unprotected files.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:35.324
A VPN can protect traffic on untrusted networks and provide an approved organizational connection,

00:00:35.324 --> 00:00:39.830
but it does not guarantee anonymity or make prohibited activity acceptable.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:42.697
Providers and destinations may still log information.

00:00:42.697 --> 00:00:48.021
Choose and use network services according to policy and the investigation's legitimate need.

00:00:48.021 --> 00:00:53.756
Separate personal accounts and identifiers from research workflows to reduce contamination and accidental disclosure.

00:00:53.756 --> 00:00:58.671
This is basic compartmentation, not permission to impersonate people, create deceptive access,

00:00:58.671 --> 00:01:00.309
or enter private communities.

00:01:00.309 --> 00:01:01.538
Minimize unnecessary exposure.

00:01:01.538 --> 00:01:06.043
Collect only what the requirement needs, avoid publishing sensitive findings broadly,

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:08.910
and restrict case material to authorized users.

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.777
Public information can still create privacy, safety,

00:01:11.777 --> 00:01:14.645
and reputational harm when aggregated or mishandled.

00:01:14.645 --> 00:01:17.512
Legal and ethical boundaries govern the workstation.

00:01:17.512 --> 00:01:22.017
Do not bypass access controls, use stolen credentials, harass, doxx, stalk,

00:01:22.017 --> 00:01:23.655
or conduct unlawful surveillance.

00:01:23.655 --> 00:01:28.980
When authority is unclear, pause and seek policy, privacy, legal, or supervisory review.
